# A test fixture: each thing that the Dialogue Manager compiler accepts and
# the server refuses. test_checks.py expects one problem for each block.
# It uses the test vocabulary of tests/helpers.py.

~ start
Guard: This cue has no end.

~ rest
while state.flag("loop")
	Looping.
% Random one.
% Random two.
Guard: [[Hi|Hello]] there.
Guard: Wait [wait=1] for it.
Guard: Tagged. [#mood=angry]
Guard: Together.
| Other: Together too.
if nobody.home("x")
	Unknown name.
if state.raise("x")
	An action in a condition.
if state.name()
	A value with brackets.
if state.flag
	A query with no brackets.
if state.flag("a", "b")
	Too many arguments.
if state.count("gold") + 1 > 2
	Arithmetic.
set state.name = "x"
do state.flag("x")
if state.checked("bad")
	A refused argument.
if gold > 1
	A bare name.
=> {{state.text("cue")}}
